{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1276, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nIn the ceremony commemorating ABC400, we want to arrange 400 people in a rectangular formation of A rows and B columns without any gaps.\nYou are given a positive integer A. Print the value of a positive integer B for which such an arrangement is possible. If there is no such positive integer B, print -1.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nA\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the value of B or -1 as specified by the problem statement.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- A is an integer between 1 and 400, inclusive.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n10\n\nSample Output 1\n\n40\r\n\nWe can arrange 400 people in 10 rows and 40 columns.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n11\n\nSample Output 2\n\n-1\n\nSample Input 3\n\n400\n\nSample Output 3\n\n1\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1308, "char_start": 1288, "quote": "Input:\n10\nOutput:\n40", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1340, "char_start": 1320, "quote": "Input:\n11\nOutput:\n-1", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1372, "char_start": 1352, "quote": "Input:\n400\nOutput:\n1", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "1e0769a47b7dd15726b4d09b7680d9dac502c8ffe10de6980b337764b02f7801", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "ef6478cf7377bcc82341626a9e211444eb34f1f2a2116865ddaa21ff04855f5b", "seq": 2}
